                <article>
                    <h1>Java</h1>
                    <p><strong>Java</strong> is a high-level, object-oriented programming language developed by Sun
                        Microsystems
                        in 1995. It is designed to be platform-independent through the Java Virtual Machine (JVM).</p>

                    <p>Java’s philosophy is <em>“Write Once, Run Anywhere,”</em> making it ideal for cross-platform
                        development.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Key Features</h2>
                    <ul class="features">
                        <li>Object-oriented programming (OOP)</li>
                        <li>Platform independence</li>
                        <li>Strong memory management</li>
                        <li>Built-in security features</li>
                        <li>Large standard library</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h2>Common Uses</h2>
                    <ul class="features">
                        <li>Android app development</li>
                        <li>Web applications</li>
                        <li>Enterprise software systems</li>
                        <li>Desktop applications</li>
                        <li>Runescape and Minecraft (the original version)</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>

